            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/tvbo/iri"/>
                <owl:minCardinality rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:minCardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/tvbo/field"/>
                <owl:maxCardinality rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:maxCardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:subClassOf>
            <owl:Restriction>
                <owl:onProperty rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/tvbo/iri"/>
                <owl:maxCardinality rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#nonNegativeInteger">1</owl:maxCardinality>
            </owl:Restriction>
        </rdfs:subClassOf>
        <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/tvbo/struct"/>
        <rdfs:label>Reference</rdfs:label>
        <skos:definition>A small typed pointer to another TVBO entity (Network, Mesh, Observation, …). The ``iri`` identifies the target via the registry; the optional ``field`` is a dotted-path subkey resolved by attribute walk on the loaded target (e.g. ``field: &apos;weight_alpha&apos;`` picks the ``weight_alpha`` named edge matrix on a Network; ``field: &apos;mesh.faces&apos;`` picks the mesh face array). Used uniformly anywhere a TVBO entity needs to point at a sub-array of another entity without inlining the data.</skos:definition>
        <skos:exactMatch rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/tvbo/Reference"/>
        <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/tvbo"/>
    </owl:Class>
    


