        <terms:description>Epileptor2D (E2D) is a phenomenological neural mass model consisting in the two-dimensional reduction (&apos;x&apos;, &apos;z&apos;) of the original Epileptor model (see Epileptor5D; Proix et al., 2014, 2017).

Note: 
------
- Equations and default parameters are taken from (Proix et al.,2014),
- The slow permittivity state-variable (z_E2D) can be modified to account for the time difference between the interictal (between seizures) and ictal (during seizure) states (see Proix et al., 2014).</terms:description>
        <terms:references rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/tvbo/studies/Proix2014"/>
        <terms:references rdf:resource="https://w3id.org/tvbo/studies/Proix2017"/>
